body:
About problem 3. ~This should actually be a separate issue, as it is not directly related to reverse maps~. It also happens for a one way mapping.
After second thoughts, I am really not sure, is it a bug?

Example:
```csharp
public class Person
{
    public string Name1 { get; set; }

    public string Name2 { get; set; }
}

[AutoMap(typeof(Person))]
public class PersonDto
{
    public string Name1 { get; set; }

    [SourceMember("Name1")]
    public string Name2 { get; set; }
}
```
When mapping a Person to a PersonDto, then the PersonDto will have Name1 and Name2 both set to the value of Person.Name1.
The alternative would be to leave Name1 in PersonDto blank, because Name1 already maps to Name2.
Anyway this would be a breaking change.
If I consider a mapping as one to many, then the current behaviour is probably intuitive.
But from the perspective of the reverse mapping, I have the problem mapping many to one.
Not sure about the right way to think about it.
